  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Boil the kettle.\n• Finely chop garlic.\n• Roughly chop Asian greens. Chop broccoli (including stalk!) into small florets. Thinly slice carrot into half-moons.\n• In a large saucepan, heat a drizzle of olive oil over high heat. Cook broccoli and carrot tossing, until tender, 4-6 minutes.\n• Add Asian greens and garlic and cook until fragrant, 1-2 minutes. Transfer to a bowl and set aside.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67f860e64264524ca9799f53/step-ac59f400.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• To saucepan, add the boiling water (2 cups for 2 people / 4 cups for 4 people), chicken stock pot, oyster sauce and the soy sauce.\n• Bring to the boil.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67f860e64264524ca9799f53/step-b52ae910.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Add udon noodles, then cover with a lid.\n• Reduce to a simmer and cook until noodles are tender, 4-5 minutes.\n• In the last minute, gently stir noodles with a fork to separate. Stir in sesame oil blend and return cooked veggies to pan.\n• Meanwhile, in a separate saucepan heat a large frying pan over medium-high heat with a drizzle of olive oil.\n• When the oil is hot, add vegetable gyozas, flat-side down, in a single layer. Cook until starting to brown, 1-2 minutes. Add the water (watch out, it may spatter!) and cover with foil or a lid.\n• Cook until the water has evaporated and gyoza are tender and softened, 4-5 minutes. Transfer to a plate.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67f860e64264524ca9799f53/step-7357c320.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide veggie gyozas and udon noodle soup with garlicky veggies between bowls.\n• Top with mixed sesame seeds to serve. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67f860e64264524ca9799f53/step-0eadad30.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
